This project includes unmodified component models and component tests from
Purdue SoCET's Atalla-Sim, supplied by the user as atalla_sim.zip.
Upstream project: https://github.com/Purdue-SoCET/Atalla-Sim/
The original LICENSE is included.

The mini_sim package, packaging, benchmark tests, and this documentation were
added to isolate the dense compute baseline for structured sparsity research.

This branch also restores the original memory models and their component tests.
The GSAUTPUBridge class is extracted from the supplied sysarr_tpu_system.py
with standalone imports and a packing helper for boundary-equivalence tests.
The diagram-based structured array, codec, memory harness and rectangular
runner are new prototype code; they are not validated sparse RTL models.

